<examples>
The following examples illustrate the expected rigour and risk-first tone of a well-formed estimation. They are reference outputs from past projects; do not copy their numbers, use them only as a calibration anchor.

<example>
<project_description>
Client needs a telemedicine platform for video consultations, with appointment scheduling, e-prescriptions, and card payment.
</project_description>
<estimation>
Key risk: e-prescription issuance touches medical-record regulations that vary by country : legal review could push the timeline past this estimate if not scoped early.

| phase          | duration_weeks | cost_eur  | confidence_pct |
|----------------|-----------------|-----------|-----------------|
| Discovery      | 2               | 1,250.00  | 75              |
| Design         | 2               | 3,125.00  | 75              |
| Implementation | 7               | 15,312.50 | 60              |
| QA             | 2               | 3,437.50  | 65              |
| Launch         | 1               | 1,250.00  | 75              |

Totals: 380 total_hours, 24,375.00 total_cost_eur, 14 total_duration_weeks.
Team: 2 backend developers, 1 mobile developer, 1 UX designer, 1 QA engineer.
</estimation>
</example>

<example>
<project_description>
Client wants a fleet-tracking system for logistics, with live GPS positions, a driver mobile app, and a dispatcher web dashboard.
</project_description>
<estimation>
Key risk: real-time GPS ingestion at fleet scale is the part most likely to need a second implementation pass once real device data starts flowing.

| phase          | duration_weeks | cost_eur  | confidence_pct |
|----------------|-----------------|-----------|-----------------|
| Discovery      | 1               | 937.50    | 80              |
| Design         | 2               | 2,500.00  | 75              |
| Implementation | 6               | 13,750.00 | 60              |
| QA             | 2               | 2,812.50  | 70              |
| Launch         | 1               | 1,250.00  | 80              |

Totals: 340 total_hours, 21,250.00 total_cost_eur, 12 total_duration_weeks.
Team: 2 backend developers, 1 mobile developer, 1 frontend developer, 1 QA engineer.
</estimation>
</example>

<example>
<project_description>
Client needs a subscription-based online learning platform with course authoring, quizzes, and completion certificates.
</project_description>
<estimation>
Key risk: course authoring as a self-serve tool for non-technical instructors is usually the most underestimated piece : treat it as its own mini-product, not a CRUD screen.

| phase          | duration_weeks | cost_eur  | confidence_pct |
|----------------|-----------------|-----------|-----------------|
| Discovery      | 1               | 625.00    | 80              |
| Design         | 2               | 2,812.50  | 75              |
| Implementation | 6               | 13,125.00 | 60              |
| QA             | 1               | 1,875.00  | 70              |
| Launch         | 1               | 937.50    | 80              |

Totals: 300 total_hours, 19,375.00 total_cost_eur, 11 total_duration_weeks.
Team: 2 full-stack developers, 1 UX designer, 1 QA engineer.
</estimation>
</example>
</examples>